      "writtenOn": "2018-11-07T18:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the goal of this CL is to only be in PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE when (drp_state[port] \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON). Is that correct? If so, the comment and \"if (...)\" here should be removed, so that tcpm_enable_drp_toggle() is always called. Or, perhaps tcpm_enable_drp_toggle() should instead be called on entry to PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE?",
      "revId": "e3ea078a17c925ca2bb88dc5c4c91bae1f6860bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "430c4c1f_67a6fe68",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3979,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-08T02:49:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should enable DRP toggle only if we decide to stay in PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE. Since the API to disable toggling has been removed, I think this is the only way to ensure we don\u0027t enable toggling if we\u0027re leaving PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE.",
      "parentUuid": "7313489e_c4e3a957",
      "revId": "e3ea078a17c925ca2bb88dc5c4c91bae1f6860bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5aa35d6_71283476",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3979,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-08T17:20:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way to disable toggling is tcpm_init(). I believe this has always been the case, and so I changed the API in CL:1194353 to try to make this clear.",
      "parentUuid": "430c4c1f_67a6fe68",
      "revId": "e3ea078a17c925ca2bb88dc5c4c91bae1f6860bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ace761b_fc7ac468",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3979,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-08T18:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this is the only way to ensure we don\u0027t enable toggling if we\u0027re leaving PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE\n\nI agree we shouldn\u0027t call tcpm_enable_drp_toggle() if we are leaving PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE.\nBut if we are leaving PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE then we won\u0027t be in this else block, will we?\nI\u0027m suggesting the \"if (drp_state[port] \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON)\" on line 3979 should be removed, because we are inside the line 3972 else block, which means next_state \u003d\u003d PD_STATE_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE, and therefore we always want to call tcpm_enable_drp_toggle().",
      "parentUuid": "a5aa35d6_71283476",
      "revId": "e3ea078a17c925ca2bb88dc5c4c91bae1f6860bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
